Third-party components

1) Build-time Rust crates. Husk is written in Rust; its dependencies are resolved
   by Cargo at build time and are not vendored here. Each crate keeps its own
   license; the build does not redistribute them.

2) glibc artifacts used to bootstrap the loader. The following files under
   `binaries/` are compiled artifacts of the GNU C Library as shipped by the
   Ubuntu 24.04 archive (package `libc6`, architecture arm64):

     binaries/ld-linux-aarch64.so.1.orig   GNU C Library dynamic loader
     binaries/libc-nop.so.6                derived from the GNU C Library shared object
     binaries/ld-embedded.so               loader built from the above

   glibc is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License v2.1 or later.
   These files are redistributed unmodified (or, in the case of
   `libc-nop.so.6`, as a locally derived binary) solely so the loader can be
   rebuilt. Corresponding source is available from the upstream GNU C Library
   and from the Ubuntu archive for the same version. They are NOT covered by the
   Apache License 2.0 that applies to Husk's own source.

   A distribution release that only needs to run Husk does not require these
   files; see `docs/RUNNING.md`.

3) Brand assets under `docs/assets/brand/` are original artwork created for this
   project and are covered by the same license as the rest of the repository.

4) No part of the LinuxHub application, its private data, or its rootfs images is
